    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by [ a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
            crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "purse (OED s.v. purse n.) (see also purs(s)e) | purse (see also porss) | wire used in making purses (OED s.v. purse n. 11) | bags for manufacturing purses | purse, a small pouch or bag of leather or other flexible material, used for carrying money on the person; originally a small bag drawn together at the mouth with a thong or strings (OED s.v. purse n. 1a), here made in Venice | a ring for closing a pouch or purse (OED s.v. pouch-ring) | purse, a small pouch or bag of leather or other flexible material, used for carrying money on the person; originally a small bag drawn together at the mouth with a thong or strings (OED s.v. purse n. 1a) | purse | purse, a small pouch or bag of leather or other flexible material, used for carrying money on the person; originally a small bag drawn together at the mouth with a thong or strings (OED s.v. purse n. 1a), here made of leather | lining for a purse | purse, money-bag; bag, pouch | purse, money-bag; bag, pouch (OED s.v. burse) | as a packing unit for wax | purse, money-bag; bag, pouch (OED s.v. burse), made of the skin of a roe: a small species of deer (capreolus capraea) inhabiting various parts of Europe and Asia (OED s.v. roe1) | purse, money-bag; bag, pouch (OED s.v. burse), here made of cloth of gold | purse, money-bag; bag, pouch, made of straw" ;
